%U A400614 50069250,50075025,50363775,57432375,500675175,508055625,509233725,5002853625,5006751750,5011689375,5019589575
%N A400614 Positions of records in A400612: integers m whose number of divisors d such that the last digit of d equals the first digit of m sets a new record.
%C A400614 The corresponding values of these records are : 1, 2, 3, 4, 8, 9, 12, 16, ...
%e A400614 4032 is a term because A400612(4032) = 9: the nine divisors d of 4032 whose last digit is equal to the first digit of 4032 are {4, 14, 24, 64, 84, 144, 224, 504, 1344}, and 9 is larger than any earlier value in A400612.
%t A400614 f[n_] := DivisorSum[n, 1 &, IntegerDigits[n][[1]] == Mod[#, 10] &]; seq[lim_] := Values[First /@ PositionIndex@ FoldList[Max, Array[f, lim]]]; seq[600000] (* _Amiram Eldar_, Oct 06 2026 *)
%Y A400614 Cf. A400612, A400613.
%Y A400614 Similar: A342833 (last digits equal), A355592 (first digits equal), A399631 (analog).
